    <TD width="3%" nowrap align="right">A:</TD>
    <TD width="1%">&nbsp;</TD>
    <TD>Generally, dividends that you receive, including dividends that are
reinvested pursuant to our dividend reinvestment plan, will be taxed as
ordinary income to the extent they are from current or accumulated
earnings and profits. We expect that some portion of your dividends
may not be subject to tax in the year in which they are received
because depreciation expense reduces the amount of taxable income but
does not reduce cash available for distribution to our shareholders.
