undiscovered or is not addressed over a period of time. Some molds may produce
airborne toxins or irritants. Concern about indoor exposure to mold has been
increasing as exposure to mold may cause a variety of adverse health effects
and symptoms, including allergic or other reactions. As a result, the presence
of significant mold at any of our properties could require us to undertake a
costly remediation program to contain or remove the mold from the affected
property. In addition, the presence of significant mold could expose us to
liability from our tenants, their employees and others if property damage or
health concerns arise.

