does not have more than 100 partners at any time during the partnership&#146;s
taxable year. In determining the number of partners in a partnership, a person
owning an interest in a flow-through entity, such as a partnership, grantor
trust or S corporation, that owns an interest in the partnership is treated as
a partner in such partnership only if (a)&nbsp;substantially all of the value of the
owner&#146;s interest in the flow-through is attributable to the flow-through
entity&#146;s interest, direct or indirect, in the partnership and (b)&nbsp;a principal
purpose of the use of the flow-through entity is to permit the partnership to
satisfy the 100 partner limitation. Hartman OP qualifies for the Private
