investing as shareholders. If this were to occur, certain contemplated
transactions between us and our trustees and other of our employees could be
deemed to be &#147;prohibited transactions.&#148; Additionally, ERISA&#146;s fiduciary
standards applicable to investments by Plans would extend to our trustees and
possibly other employees as Plan fiduciaries with respect to investments made
by us, and the requirement that Plan Assets be held in trust could be deemed to
