<P align="left" style="font-size: 10pt"><B>Part I. Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN)</B>


<P align="left" style="font-size: 10pt"><B>Enter your TIN in the appropriate box. </B>If you
are a <B>resident alien </B>and you do not have and
are not eligible to get an SSN, your TIN is
your IRS individual taxpayer identification
number (ITIN). Enter it in the social
security number box. If you do not have an
ITIN, see <B>How to get a TIN </B>below.



<P align="left" style="font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are a <B>sole proprietor </B>and you
have an EIN, you may enter either your SSN or
EIN. However, the IRS prefers that you use
your SSN.


<P align="left" style="font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are a single-owner <B>LLC </B>that is
disregarded as an entity separate from its
